{"name":"Roycroft Pewter","hex":"#616564","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pewter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alloy of approximately 93–98% tin and 1–2% copper, and the balance of antimony.","An alloy of tin and lead."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark, dull grey colour, like that of the metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pewter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roycroft","blocks":[{"text":"Roycroft was a reformist community of craft workers and artists which formed part of the Arts and Crafts movement in the United States. Elbert Hubbard founded the community in 1895, in the village of East Aurora, New York, near Buffalo. Participants were known as Roycrofters. The work and philosophy of the group, often referred to as the Roycroft movement, had a strong influence on the development of American architecture and design in the early 20th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Roycroft_Copper_Shop.jpg/330px-Roycroft_Copper_Shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roycroft","wikidata":"Q2171198"},{"title":"Pewter","blocks":[{"text":"Pewter is a malleable metal alloy consisting of tin (85–99%), antimony, copper (2%), bismuth, and sometimes silver. In the past, it was an alloy of tin and as much as 40% lead, but most modern pewter, in order to prevent lead poisoning, is not made with lead. Pewter has a low melting point, around 170–230 °C (338–446 °F), depending on the exact mixture of metals. The word pewter is possibly a variation of \"spelter\", a term for zinc alloys."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pewter","wikidata":"Q852372"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/500px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/1280px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Roycroft_printing_press.jpg/500px-Roycroft_printing_press.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golding Pearl letterpress used by the Roycrofters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoycroft_printing_press.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/1280px-A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-A_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A door of the Chapel (not a religious building but a guild hall)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_door_of_the_Chapel%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/1280px-Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg/500px-Roycroft_Inn%2C_Lobby_bar%2C_Roycroft_Campus.jpg?utm_sou